The implementation must ensure the stored image reference is resolvable by the application's image loader, either through an appropriate image-serving mechanism or a documented authenticated image fetcher.

Do not expose spreadsheet-owner credentials or private Google Drive access tokens.

Do not make uploaded images publicly accessible without the business owner's explicit configuration and understanding of the exposure.

If a private authenticated asset-fetch mechanism is required, implement it without introducing a second business datastore.

## 10.6 Image precedence

The priority is:

```text
1. User-uploaded image
2. User-pasted image URL
3. Automatically generated Bing thumbnail
4. Neutral placeholder
```

A manual override must not be replaced by automatic image generation.

The hierarchy applies to the currently chosen image; the application does not need multiple image columns.

## 10.7 Image persistence

Products.photo_url is the authoritative image reference.

Store only one URL.

Do not store image bytes in Google Sheets.

Do not introduce additional image-source columns.

When the user chooses a manual image:

- Replace photo_url with the chosen URL.
- Preserve it during subsequent product edits.
- Do not regenerate it automatically.

When no manual override exists:

- The default URL may be updated when barcode or product name changes.

To distinguish an existing automatic URL from an override without adding schema columns, compare the existing photo_url with the URL generated from the previous barcode and product name.

If the existing URL matches the previous generated default, it may be regenerated.

Otherwise, preserve the image URL as a manual override.

## 10.8 Removing an override

Provide:

**Use Automatic Image**

When selected:

1. Remove the current manual choice from the product form.
2. Regenerate the default image URL.
3. Attempt loading the new candidate.
4. Display the preview or fallback.
5. Save the resulting photo_url on confirmation.

Do not delete a previously uploaded binary object as an unintended side effect of simply changing product details.

## 10.9 Image editing UX

The product form should show:

```text
Product Photo

[ Image Preview ]

[ Use Automatic ] [ Paste URL ] [ Upload ]
```

Use a clean and touch-friendly arrangement.

Avoid unnecessary dialogs.

On successful image selection, update the preview immediately.

Use concise error messages.

Examples:

```text
Image unavailable
Invalid image URL
Upload failed
Image updated
Using automatic image
```

## 10.10 Image performance

- Use Coil.
- Cache images.
- Avoid repeated network requests.
- Use a fixed or bounded image-preview size.
- Preserve layout while images load.
- Provide fallback placeholders.
- Avoid downloading oversized image assets.
- Do not refresh every product image on every screen navigation.
- Cancel obsolete image requests when inputs change.
- Do not regenerate manual URLs.

## 10.11 Image tests

Test:

- Barcode + name combination.
- UTF-8 encoding.
- Space-to-plus encoding.
- Leading-zero barcode preservation.
- Special characters in names.
- Empty barcode.
- Empty product name.
- Both fields empty.
- Default URL generation.
- Broken thumbnail URL.
- Non-image response.
- Manual URL replacement.
- Image upload.
- Manual URL persistence.
- Automatic regeneration after relevant edits.
- Image cache behavior.
- Save despite failed image loading.

The default image flow must work without requiring a paid image-search API.

